---
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/learn.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="Renku skills for other agents" description="Install Renku skills separately for Cursor and other agents that support local commands and Agent Skills.">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="learn-page" id="top">
    <header class="container learn-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Agent setup</p>
        <h1>Skills for other agents</h1>
        <p class="lede">Renku automatically sets up plugins for Claude and Codex. For another agent, install the skills separately and choose its installation scope explicitly.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/download/">Back to installation</a>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="container reading-layout">
      <aside class="reading-nav"><p class="eyebrow">Installation guide</p><a href="#requirements">Before you start</a><a href="#project">Project skills</a><a href="#global">Global skills</a><a href="#updates">Verify and update</a></aside>
      <div class="reading-content">
        <section class="lesson-section" id="requirements">
          <h2>Before you start</h2>
          <p>Install Renku first and confirm <code>renku about</code> works in a terminal. Your agent must support local command execution and Agent Skills. The available tools and media review experience depend on the agent.</p>
          <p>The commands below use the independent <a href="https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills">skills tool</a>. Install Node.js and Git according to that tool’s requirements; Renku does not bundle it. Running <code>npx skills</code> may download the tool and ask for confirmation.</p>
          <p>Find your agent’s identifier in the <a href="https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills#supported-agents">supported agents list</a>. The examples use <code>cursor</code>; replace that value with your agent’s identifier. Avoid selecting all agents.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lesson-section" id="project">
          <h2>Install for one project</h2>
          <p>Open a terminal in the folder your agent will work in, then run:</p>
          <pre><code>npx skills add GoRenku/studio-skills --agent cursor --skill '*' --copy</code></pre>
          <p>Choose project scope if prompted, review the destination, and confirm. Copy mode installs regular files rather than symbolic links. Keep your agent working in that folder so it can discover the skills.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lesson-section" id="global">
          <h2>Install across projects</h2>
          <p>Use global scope only if the tool lists global installation support for your agent. For example, Cursor supports:</p>
          <pre><code>npx skills add GoRenku/studio-skills --agent cursor --skill '*' --copy --global</code></pre>
          <p>Project-only agents, including PromptScript, must use project scope. Do not add <code>--global</code> for them.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lesson-section" id="updates">
          <h2>Verify and update</h2>
          <p>Start a new agent conversation and check that the Renku skills are available. Begin with <code>movie-director</code>, using your agent’s skill interface.</p>
          <p>To refresh the skills, rerun the same installation command with the same agent and scope. <code>renku update skills</code> refreshes the Claude/Codex plugins; it does not manage other agents’ skills.</p>
          <p>Existing skill files are retained when you update Renku. If you previously installed both loose skills and a plugin for the same agent, review duplicates using that agent’s own controls.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
